text:
claire: FYI customer Acme (acct 4321) reports intermittent invalid JSON from JSON mode, started ~today. Sample response below.

claire: ```json
{"id":123, "name":"widget" "price":9.99}
```

claire: We see this ~1-2% of requests, mostly at higher token lengths. They get a parse error client-side.

ben: @claire can you paste the exact request payload + headers (model, temp, max_tokens)?

claire: sanitized payload:

```json
{ "model": "open-redwood-1.0", "prompt": "extract product as JSON", "temperature": 0.2, "max_tokens": 450, "json_schema": { /* redacted */ } }
```

claire: curl repro:

```bash
curl -s -X POST https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer <REDACTED>" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"model":"open-redwood-1.0","input":"...","mode":"json"}'
```

ben: ok thanks. initial ideas: 1) client-side tolerant parse: regex to extract first {...} block: `/({[\s\S]*})/m` 2) deterministic retries with backoff: 500ms, 1s, 2s (stop after 3) 3) post-process: trim trailing garbage after last `}` and before first `{` 4) server side: re-ask/self-heal prompt and low temp.

ben: re-ask prompt example:

```text
You must return valid JSON that matches the schema. If the model output is not valid JSON, only output the corrected JSON object and nothing else. If you cannot, output: "__PARSE_FAIL__".
```

alice: for support playbook: tell customer to set temperature 0 and enable retries with exponential backoff; provide regex fallback snippet. Also ask for sample failing response + request id.

claire: gave them small patch: client code example for fallback:

```js
async function fetchJson(req){
  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    const res = await callApi(req)
    try{ return JSON.parse(res)
    }catch(e){
      // attempt quick cleanup
      const match = res.match(/({[\s\S]*})/m)
      if(match) return JSON.parse(match[0])
      await sleep(500 * Math.pow(2,i))
    }
  }
  throw new Error('parse_failed')
}
```

diego: @ben can you check runtime logs for `request_id: 0f3a` around 12:04 UTC? maybe a truncation/stream chunk boundary.

ben: will grep logs and try to repro with long outputs. If it's stream chunking, we may need to change chunk flush or ensure finalization token marks.

parsebot: Incident created: #INC-2026-482 (assigned to ben)

ben: I'll take it. provisional mitigation: server-side re-ask on invalid parse for hosted customers, toggle for enterprise. Will update here when root cause found :eyes:

alice: thanks team :thumbsup:

claire: customer accepted temp workaround, will keep an eye and send failing responses if seen :pray:
